# Trivy ignore list — CVEs that are acknowledged but not actionable.
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line, optionally with comment.
# Reference: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#by-finding-ids

# CVE-2026-33671 — Picomatch ReDoS via crafted extglob patterns
# Affected: next/dist/compiled/picomatch (vendored into Next.js 16.2.6)
# Why ignored: vendored copy compiled into Next.js, not steerable via
# package-lock or npm overrides. Used internally by Next.js for file-path
# matching at build time, never receives user-controlled input.
# Re-evaluate when Next.js bumps the vendored version.
CVE-2026-33671

# CVE-2026-48818 — Starlette SSRF + NTLM credential theft via UNC paths in StaticFiles
# CVE-2026-54283 — Starlette request.form() limits silently ignored (DoS)
# Affected: starlette 0.52.1 (pulled in via fastapi)
# Why ignored: fixed versions (1.1.0 / 1.3.1) do not exist on PyPI yet;
# no actionable upgrade path available. Re-evaluate when starlette releases the patch.
CVE-2026-48818
CVE-2026-54283

# CVE-2026-14257 — brace-expansion DoS via crafted brace patterns
# Affected: brace-expansion 1.1.16 (via minimatch@3 in the ESLint toolchain) and
# 5.0.7 (via @typescript-eslint/typescript-estree). Both are dev-only build-time
# dependencies, never invoked on user-controlled input at runtime.
# Why ignored: the 1.x branch has no patched release (latest 1.x is the flagged
# 1.1.16); patching it would force minimatch@3 onto an incompatible major and
# cascade an upgrade of the whole legacy ESLint toolchain.
# Re-evaluate when brace-expansion ships a 1.x fix or the ESLint deps are bumped.
CVE-2026-14257

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 — msgpack out-of-bounds read/crash on Unpacker reuse
# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools path traversal in PackageIndex
# Affected (per Trivy): provibackend image, msgpack "1.1.2" / setuptools "70.3.0"
# Why ignored: false positive. requirements.txt pins msgpack>=1.2.1 and
# setuptools>=78.1.1, and the Dockerfile additionally force-reinstalls both
# with --no-deps right after the main install. Verified directly against the
# built image (not just the build log): `docker run provibackend:scan pip show
# msgpack setuptools` reports 1.2.2 / 84.0.0, and a full filesystem search
# (`find / -iname '*.dist-info'`) finds exactly one dist-info for each, at the
# patched version — no stale metadata anywhere. Trivy nonetheless reports the
# GHSA's earliest-affected version as "Installed Version" for both findings.
# Re-evaluate (and drop these two lines) after upgrading Trivy past v0.70.0.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
